    <div class="meadow-prose">
      <h2>Between now and then.</h2>
      <p>Some of the best projects start from what the client already knows about their land. While we reach back, you might jot down a few things we always ask about on the first call.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>How much sun does the site get — and where does it fall in the morning vs. afternoon?</li>
        <li>What's been planted there before, and what died out?</li>
        <li>Which hours of the day do you actually spend outside now, and which would you like to?</li>
        <li>Anything particular you want to keep — a tree, a view, a memory?</li>
        <li>What's your honest install budget range? We'd rather know up front than choreograph around it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>None of it is required, and we'll walk through all of it when we meet. But if you want to arrive with notes, those are the questions that move the first conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

